4017 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424017 1077 "selection" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424017 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424008 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424017 1079 #uuid "d8116051-5575-52c2-b4e3-895e85818216" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424018 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424017 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424018 1069 "q-136921" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424018 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424018 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $b$ above. If the normal equation corresponding to the system $Ax=b$ is given below, what is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 20 \\\\ 20 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424018 1072 #uuid "130f7ccc-d087-5052-915e-6df794e733bd" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424018 1074 "The normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}10 & 20 \\\\ 20 & 40\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+40+4=54.\n$$" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424019 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424016 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424019 1069 "q-136920" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424019 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424019 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,[\\begin{aligned}20 & 10 & a \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5 \\\\ c & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear equations and its corresponding normal equation shown above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424019 1072 #uuid "4cb13173-852b-58a2-8c1f-3d6511a05fac" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true] [17592186424019 1074 "First, we write our system in matrix form as $Ax=b,$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe normal equation corresponding to $Ax=b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 & 10 & 10 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=10+4+10=24.\n$$" 13194139534517 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-06a52bea-6ee1-5ba3-91a9-fa2c837b2777" 17592186424006 "answer-1c6dd795-91e5-55e1-984a-5549435634d1" 17592186424007 "answer-20388d9f-ef78-593d-a86d-57d7b9255118" 17592186424008 "answer-6235969c-cd1d-5e61-9e7a-9328ddcaeab8" 17592186424009 "answer-75f256ad-47a3-5c49-a78e-1c5ae0257228" 17592186424010 "answer-8612d6bf-1d46-5e5b-b